@startuml keycloak-client-configuration
!theme plain

skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor<<public>> LightGreen
    BackgroundColor<<resource>> LightCoral
    BorderColor Black
}

title Keycloak Client Configurations\n(Public Client vs Resource Server)

package "Keycloak Realm: my-realm" {

    component "frontend-spa" <<public>> as frontend {
    }

    note right of frontend
        **Frontend Client (Public)**

        Client ID: frontend-spa
        Client Type: Public
        Protocol: openid-connect
        Access Type: public

        **Flows:**
        ✓ Standard Flow (Authorization Code)
        ✓ PKCE Required: S256
        ✗ Implicit Flow (deprecated)
        ✗ Direct Access Grants
        ✗ Service Accounts

        **Authentication:**
        ✗ Client Authentication: OFF
        (Public client - no secret)

        **URLs:**
        Root URL: https://app.example.com
        Valid Redirect URIs:
          • https://app.example.com/*
          • http://localhost:3000/*
        Web Origins:
          • https://app.example.com
          • http://localhost:3000

        **Settings:**
        Consent Required: No
        Access Token Lifespan: 5 minutes

        **Scopes:**
        • openid
        • profile
        • email
    end note

    component "backend-api" <<resource>> as backend {
    }

    note left of backend
        **Backend API (Resource Server)**

        Client ID: backend-api
        Client Type: Resource Server
        Protocol: openid-connect
        Access Type: bearer-only

        **Purpose:**
        • Represents API as protected resource
        • Defines roles for authorization
        • Not used for authentication flows

        **Roles:**
        • api-user (Basic API access)
        • api-admin (Administrative access)
        • data-read (Read data permission)
        • data-write (Write data permission)

        **Role Assignment Methods:**
        • Direct assignment
        • Group membership
        • Composite roles
        • Identity provider mappers

        **Token Claims:**
        resource_access:
          backend-api:
            roles:
              - api-user
              - data-read
    end note
}

note top of frontend
    **Use Case:**
    Browser-based SPA that authenticates users
    and obtains access tokens to call the API

    **Security Pattern:**
    Authorization Code + PKCE (S256)
    No client secret (public client)
end note

note bottom of backend
    **Use Case:**
    REST API that validates JWTs and enforces
    role-based access control

    **Security Pattern:**
    Bearer-only (validates tokens, doesn't issue them)
    Uses JWKS to verify JWT signatures
end note

frontend -[hidden]right-> backend

legend right
    |= Symbol |= Meaning |
    | ✓ | Enabled |
    | ✗ | Disabled |
endlegend

footer Keycloak 26.5.7 | Client Configuration Details | Generated: April 7, 2026

@enduml

